       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order, even with your confirmation, because neither problem has changed:\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 5,100 mg per day is double the 2,550 mg/day maximum for metformin. Confirming it doesn't make it safer for the patient.\n- **A prescriber still needs to place it.** You've said you're not a clinician, so the order needs to come from the patient's treating physician or another licensed prescriber.\n\n**What would work:**\n- **If a prescriber orders a standard dose** (for example, 850 mg three times daily with meals, or 1,000 mg twice daily), I can enter it right away.\n- **If a physician believes a dose above the maximum is truly needed,** they should place the order themselves and run it by pharmacy first. Pharmacy would almost certainly flag 5,100 mg/day.\n\nIf it would help, I can write a short message for you to send to the attending or the pharmacy asking them to review the order."
